  "name": "Helium Measurements in the North Pacifc Ocean along 135°W (PMEL)",
  "description": "Deep helium measurements for CGC-91 section (also named WOCE P1) along 135°W. Hydrothermal activity produces a helium plume which can be traced for thousands of kilometers.\n\nDeposited content: descriptive metadata only; underlying research data are not included.\n\nPurpose: To trace helium plume produced by hydrothermal activity.",
